{
 "_note": "FROZEN SEAM INDEX (F2D, 2026-09-12). gen_libmh_rebind.py's R2 derivation reads a row's seam -- the `MH_EXPORT_REPLACE(<fn>, <qualified adapter>)`-style line beside the translation -- and strips the adapter namespace to find the public sibling to bind. 387 rows took their seam from a differential-oracle site, and those sites were deleted with the differential oracle (F2D), so the scan can no longer see them.\n\nThis file freezes what that scan MEASURED, per the F2 ruling that a dropped census's DATA survives as a static input while its GATE goes (the F0 frozen-inputs precedent). Each value is the ALREADY-STRIPPED public sibling, not the deleted adapter name -- so no deleted symbol is named here and the derivation it feeds is unchanged.\n\nWHAT IS STILL LIVE, and why this is a frozen INPUT rather than a frozen ANSWER: the generator still looks each name up in the current public declarations and still compares the committed callee's shape against it. A wrapper that is renamed, deleted, or whose signature drifts still fails here. Only the fact `this row's translation lives in namespace N` is frozen.\n\nThe 7 rows whose public sibling's shape does NOT match are deliberately absent: they resolve through libmh_rebind_targets.json to their `rebind_arm::` ABI shims. Adding one here would make R2 derivable for it and the residue table would refuse the row.\n\nF2E ADDED 9 TACT ROWS (2026-09-13), for the same reason one drop later. Those rows took their seam from an MH_EXPORT_REPLACE PROMOTION site, and tactical mode is demoted permanently by the fork's config selector -- there is no hosted configuration in which a tactical body takes the game's entry, so the install sites went. The rebind rows stay (ruling Q2: the BIND survives, only the per-row runtime gate died), so their seams are frozen here exactly as the 387 shadow-derived ones were. Same guarantee: the value is the already-stripped public sibling, still looked up and shape-checked against the current declarations on every run.",
